      "issue": "8cf73d9d-217b-4648-a810-5b9d68b1d72a",
      "rule": "java:S4502",
      "rationale": "Reviewed against the actual credential transport on 2026-10-08. Spring Security is stateless; form login and HTTP Basic are disabled; no authentication cookie/session is accepted. React explicitly sets Authorization from memory with credentials=omit. CORS allows only local frontend origins with allowCredentials=false. The exercised Postman collection verifies cookie-only requests return 401, untrusted-origin preflight returns 403, and local bearer preflight succeeds. Ignoring CSRF only for /api is appropriate for this transport. Revisit before introducing any automatically attached credential. See outputs/04_Decisions/01_Authentication.md.",
      "commentSaved": true,
      "transitionStatus": 200
    },
    {
      "issue": "5d1f0b6d-afb8-4b59-9149-2b649fe6e31f",
      "rule": "javascript:S6845",
      "rationale": "Reviewed the real scrolling interaction on 2026-10-08. This named native section is an overflow-x:auto table scroll region. tabIndex=0 intentionally makes native arrow-key scrolling available to keyboard users. The browser test focuses it and verifies ArrowRight changes scrollLeft on tablet; the page itself has no horizontal overflow. Removing focusability would prevent access in browsers that do not automatically focus scroll containers. MDN overflow accessibility recommends a focusable named region: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/overflow . This is a native scroll interaction, not an inert decorative element.",
      "commentSaved": true,
      "transitionStatus": 200
    }
